! Bmad translation of Genesis's benchmark/Benchmark1-SASE/Aramis.lat, for the steady-state
! FEL benchmark. See fel_ss_test.f90 for how it is used.
!
! The undulator segments appear as drift placeholders named UND: fel_ss_test intercepts
! every element whose name starts with UND and applies the FEL step to it; only the length
! matters here (the FEL parameters aw, lambdau, kx, ky, helical come from the program's
! namelist input). Everything else -- D1, QF, QD, D2 -- is tracked by Bmad. A real FEL
! element type with its own tracking method is a later deliverable; this placeholder scheme
! is the smallest thing that exercises the seam.
!
! The reference energy: Genesis's gamma0 = 11357.82 times Bmad's electron rest mass. The
! FEL physics uses gamma0 directly from the namelist; the lattice's p0c only sets the scale
! of Bmad's normalized transverse momenta, and the conversion routines read it back from
! the element, so the two sides stay individually self-consistent (see fel_beam_mod).
!
! Genesis's quadrupole k1 = 2 m^-2 is the geometric strength at the reference energy;
! Bmad's k1 has the same meaning. The chromatic behavior then differs at the model level:
! Genesis scales the focusing per particle by gamma0/gammaz (TrackBeam.cpp:26,69), Bmad by
! p0/p. The two differ by ~4e-9 relative at this energy, quantified in the benchmark README.

no_digested
parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
parameter[e_tot] = 11357.82 * m_electron

beginning[beta_a] = 10   ! Placeholder Twiss; tracking here does not use lattice Twiss.
beginning[beta_b] = 10

! The FEL element proper (deliverable 9): a real wiggler with tracking_method = custom
! (Bmad's semantics for program-supplied tracking, which fel_track_test provides). The
! FEL parameters derive from the attributes: aw = c*b_max/(k_u*m_e c^2) for a helical
! device (rms convention), so b_max below encodes aw = 0.84853 exactly as an expression
! in Bmad's own constants; helicity from field_calc; period from l_period.
UND: wiggler, l = 3.99, l_period = 0.015, field_calc = helical_model, &
     b_max = 0.84853 * (twopi / 0.015) * m_electron / c_light, &
     tracking_method = custom, num_steps = 1
D1: drift, l = 0.44
D2: drift, l = 0.24
QF: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = 2.0
QD: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = -2.0

FODO: line = (UND, D1, QF, D2, UND, D1, QD, D2)
ARAMIS: line = (6*FODO)

use, ARAMIS
